To use the Virtual Fly Brain Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool, access it at vfb3-mcp.virtualflybrain.org and follow the quick start guide for setup with Claude Desktop, GitHub Copilot, or other MCP-compatible clients. Configure the tool by adding the VFB3-MCP server with the provided settings.

```
{
"mcpServers": {
"virtual-fly-brain": {
"type": "http",
"url": "https://vfb3-mcp.virtualflybrain.org",
"tools": ["*"]
}
}
}
```

Then, test the connection by asking questions like "Get information about the neuron " or "Search for terms related to medulla in the fly brain". VFB provides access to three main capabilities: term information queries, term search, and query execution, and supports various datasets, including FAFB-FlyWire, Male-CNS optic lobe, FlyCircuit, and Hemibrain.
